WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.610
W-What did you say?

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.580
This is not a human.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.120
It is a Disckonian.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.930
Sade!

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.890
Stand back!

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.980
I am thankful in many ways.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.930
Thankful I could meet the blasphemer here.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.340
Thankful that the blasphemer is not a citizen of this planet.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.470
My death will be repentance for my shameful actions.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.970
But before that, I have something I must do.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.580
I swear on the pride of our race!

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.120
I will kill you!

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.900
Presently, there are hundreds of alien species coming and going,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.190
living their lives on Earth.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.780
Species that come in peace...

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.510
Aggressive, warlike species...

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:11.940
All kinds of alien species coexist with us, maintaining a precarious balance.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.980
And among them exist dangerous races

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:19.540
that start intergalactic wars at the slightest provocation!

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.340
So, the attack begins?

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.080
The situation couldn't be worse.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.550
The towns entrance is adorned with a cow's skull

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:41.510
It's fine that the law is decided by the strongest,

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.500
But this simple feeling will not be enough to fulfill you

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.980
Everyone will definitely revolt and shortly disappear

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:57.260
That's a shocking bloody picture

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.410
I'm feeling nauseous

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:12.620
Holding my head, I board the subway

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:23.060
Righteous way of living, righteous way of dying

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:33.510
Who on earth knows or what the hell can show me?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.700
Cold finger girl

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.850
Sit Down

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.970
When their lives are in danger,

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.970
it is said they instinctively go into a coma-like state.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.510
Thanatosis.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.640
It is an evolutionary defense mechanism.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.640
In other words, they fake death?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.660
This apartment is non-smoking, buddy.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.900
The problem is that faking death is considered shameful to them.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.070
Why?

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.220
Because if you're strong you shouldn't have to play dead.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.160
Doin' something like that just proves you're weak, right?

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.120
That is essentially correct.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.620
Ecologically speaking,

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:46.320
evolutionary development of thanatosis is proof of the existence of a stronger predator.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.540
The Disckonians, after a long struggle for survival, wiped out their mortal enemy,

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.470
and stood at the top of their planet's food chain.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.600
In other words, it is an ability that reminds them of their unpleasant past.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.280
Furthermore,

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.750
they believe that an embarrassment for one of them is an embarrassment for their entire race.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.240
They will then eliminate whomever caused their embarrassment.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.290
But that's...

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.110
They're like yakuza aliens.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.940
So, basically...

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.950
I'm the Prince of Dogura?!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.450
You're surprised about that <i>now</i>?

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.870
Yukitaka, bring me coffee.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.500
He likes using people, doesn't he?

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.910
Colin, hail the escape pod immediately.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.730
And send an emergency signal to the mothership.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.910
But if we make contact from here,

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.320
that would violate the Protection of Developing Planets Regulation...

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.090
Now is not the time to be worrying about that, fool!

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.850
That really is...

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.130
Huh? It's not activating.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:42.910
What?

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.060
It looks like they've already made the first move.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.180
Telling us there's no running away, are you?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.910
You can hear me, yes?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.640
You have until sunset.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.660
Hand over the person responsible to us.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.290
With him, our hand will not strike.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.230
He is nothing but a commoner, yes?

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.960
Not bad, I think, as bargains go...

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.010
Captain...

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.550
He knows full well that he is not a commoner.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.290
Prince...

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.480
Looks like it.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.680
Understood. I'll go.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.100
Everything will be settled if I sacrifice myself, yes?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.970
I'd like nothing better, if I could!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:33.490
But as long as the fate of the galactic conference lies in your hands, I can't!

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.140
Ah, well.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.500
In this case,

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:40.160
I'll have to use the fact that they are forbidden from harming Earthlings against them.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:44.290
You will make for excellent hostages!

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.150
Indeed!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.060
If we cooperate with the Earthlings, it'll be possible for us to escape!

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.060
Cooperate?

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:53.040
But how do we escape using them as shields?

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.190
Shields?

00:05:54.190 --> 00:06:00.180
Captain, I think they would be better as witnesses during negotiations.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.180
Witnesses?

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.600
Even if they play nice with Earthlings,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.880
anyone from other planets is no good with them at all.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.510
Do we have room for negotiations?

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.150
Indeed...

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.810
Don't just decide this on your own!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.580
Listen up, Slick!

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.780
We ain't gonna be your shields nor your witnesses, got it?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.270
You want there to be a little accident here, brat?

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.160
Have you made your decision?

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.860
I do not know who you are protecting,

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:29.230
but is he really worth us escalating to full-on war?

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:29.880
Wait!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.590
There are humans here.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:37.250
These humans and us really get along.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.640
They said, "we can't watch as our best friend is killed!" and want to move...

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.950
Out! Get out!

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:44.210
You idiot!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.840
Understood.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.860
We will take you away from in front of the poor humans.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:54.380
You really <i>do</i> have a death wish!

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.710
We're <i>best friends</i>, right?

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.980
You gonna kill your <i>best friend</i>?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.700
Enough, you two!

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:08.040
It's somewhat of a long shot, however...

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.920
The Disckonian's weak point?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.850
Yes.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.830
The prince was heading to the intergalactic conference,

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.700
therefore he had amassed a great deal of data on various life forms.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:23.140
I'm sure that data on the Disckonians should be among them.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:27.100
So, if we can get his memories back, perhaps...

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:28.350
Is that right?

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:28.980
Yes.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.090
What is it?

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.940
Everyone gossiping about me?

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:36.450
Do you even realize the position that you're in?

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:39.690
I believe that my maternal grandfather once said:

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:43.390
"The best way to retrieve lost memories is to recreate a shock"

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:45.700
"equal to the one that caused them to be lost..."

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.310
Stand still!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:49.880
That's just superstition!

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.390
That's an old-wives' tale used only by barbarians with no sense of sentient rights!

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.960
I know! I know all too well!

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.280
I don't want to do this either!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.690
But this situation requires haste, Prince!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.550
You seem oddly pleased, however...

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.270
There is no-no-no-no-no-no...

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:08.930
...time!

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.810
So? Memories returned?

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.870
Uh... Duh...

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.370
Not yet.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.320
Oh, too bad!

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.900
Prince, forgive me!

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.990
Please forgive me!

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.270
Huh?

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.360
Sade! How about now?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.160
Not yet.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.240
Okay! I'm gettin' into it now!

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.980
Prince! Just a little more! A little more!

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.660
Does the captain have some sort of grudge?

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.050
Yes...

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:49.680
The prince has a genius level intellect, but his personality is extremely troubled.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:55.030
All he does is play pranks, making the citizens suffer,

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:58.360
instead of using his intelligence to support them.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:02.760
Captain Craft is the only one to ever criticize him.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.240
After that...

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:12.280
He was forced to do the worst possible tasks just to harass him.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.250
So cold...

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:14.830
I see.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.540
I think I can understand.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.420
But...

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.880
Give up? Give up?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.380
But right now we have no choice than to rely on the prince's knowledge.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.350
Knowledge, huh?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.310
A crystal data system!

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.300
I see! He had one of these?

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.000
Damn! It's not enough!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.360
Sunset!

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.410
It is time.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.430
Begin!

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.910
We are now breaking in.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.010
Here it is.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:02.500
What an incredible amount of data!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.510
Where's the part about Disckonians?

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.380
Wait a moment.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:22.910
Amazing.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:25.690
There's so much information on the secretive Disckonians...

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.480
There's no time to be impressed!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.290
Is there info that'll get us out of here? I don't care what!

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.560
They've entered Tsutsui-kun's room...

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.580
Isn't there anything else?

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.260
Right.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.510
There is.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.180
T-This is...

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.290
What? Just do it already.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.070
But...

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.020
Where are they?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.050
In the room next door?

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.320
Hurry!

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.620
I can't!

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.350
I can't view this data!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.010
Why not?

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:11.300
If I see this I'll be killed!

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.190
Move it! I'll do it!

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:24.360
What's this?

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:25.550
I don't know.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.340
What... is this?

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.100
No...

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:35.640
What?

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.110
What's going on, you people?

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:39.140
What exactly is it displaying?

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.370
You're...

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:06.810
Tsutsui-kun...

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.800
You have nowhere left to run or hide...

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.590
Hand him over to us.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.310
You gonna kill him?

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.830
Yes, of course.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.610
Sorry, but I like cats.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.450
If you want him, you're gonna have to go through me!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.060
I see...

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:47.780
In that case...

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:52.630
"Instead of the prince, I'll be satisfied by your three lives!"

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:02.410
Enough... Enough already.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:06.970
Um, Lafferty-kun, was it?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.270
Did someone tell him my name?

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:10.970
No...

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.580
So, how should I respond to this?

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.720
Maybe throw down my life?

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.200
Die in service to Planet Dogura?

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:22.090
What the hell are you talking about?

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.240
Enough! That's enough.

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:30.250
Um... Have you noticed already?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.000
Yeah...

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.630
This whole damn thing was his plan, right?

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:38.310
Ack! We're busted!

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.360
So lame! I punched a hole through the wall and everything!

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.090
What's going on?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:44.810
Beats me.

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:48.490
Colin, can you play it back so that they can view it?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.810
Please wait a moment.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.450
The cat?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:03.220
Everything is being recorded in a camera the prince hid in that cat.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.900
The Prince of Dogura's in big trouble!

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.670
Exciting! The Prince of Dogura's in big trouble and we've got to rescue him right away plan!

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.640
- featuring Craft, Sade, and Colin!

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.960
March 28th
(JST)

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:20.740
Testing the loyalty of your servants?

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.740
Agent Sade
5 years as the prince's bodyguard

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.740
Captain Craft
10 years as the prince's bodyguard

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.740
Agent Colin
1 year as the prince's bodyguard

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:21.570
Yes.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.390
Will you assist me?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.140
Sounds interesting.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.580
But I won't do it for nothing...

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.420
The demand of the Disckonians!

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:33.680
Observe the arriving baseball scholarship student

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.680
Tsutsui Yukitaka

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:34.200
It is forbidden in our race to get within 1000 paces,

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.850
but everyone's said they really want to see him.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.400
Understood. We have a deal.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.560
March 29th
(JST)

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.430
Brought to you by Disckonian Shouji-san

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.270
The plan begins

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.270
Crash landing

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:48.820
March 30th
(JST)

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:53.780
Successfully broke into Tsutsui Yukitaka's apartment

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:01.050
Amenbo Akaina A-I-U-E-O

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.330
Set up spy cameras - Check

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.330
Learn the local language - Check

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.500
All goes according to plan

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.790
March 31st
(JST)

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.600
Who are you?

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.000
Face off with Tsutsui Yukitaka

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.000
That's my line!

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.680
An excitable stooge

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.000
I'm Edogawa Miho.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:23.500
I know this isn't much, but...

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.520
The neighbour, Edogawa Miho, appears

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.690
A female whose face
screams out "XXXX me!"

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.480
What the hell was written there?!

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.720
I can't translate it.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:30.570
Realized a mistake was made with the moving camera

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.660
Because there aren't any wild ones near here.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.760
I see.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.860
Camera change

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.510
I believe this is called a "cat".

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:41.800
A stray cat is camera #2

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:41.800
This'll do.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.880
He's still looking.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.550
Now that I think about it, I don't know where to go.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:47.010
But if I return now it'll be annoying.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.130
April 1st
(JST)

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.880
Crystal data to Conan Research Laboratory

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.880
I'm prevented from telling my daughter, however.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:57.720
Some organizations know about aliens
coming to Earth, apparently.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:02.010
He was pleased after I showed him the crystal
data system and my parrot (camera #1).

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.230
With the plan already in action,
he promises to help.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:08.500
Send the two of them to Miho's room.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.540
I'm sure he'll stick his neck out for you.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:14.620
But, my daughter sure has blossomed lately...

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.360
A female that screams
"XXXX me", indeed!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.820
Make Yukitaka think I was attacked

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.240
Toy with Yukitaka's emotions in various ways

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.240
Simpleton

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.450
March 2nd
(JST)

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:24.750
Decide on who plays dead

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.670
I pulled out my front teeth just for this day!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.920
Disckonian

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.920
Lafferty-kun

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.530
You sure about this?

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.880
I always wanted to play dead once!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:31.710
Choose a secret password

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:36.600
So I just need to close in on them, saying "I'll be satisfied by your three lives!"

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.890
Test the three's loyalty

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.140
Backed into a corner

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:44.640
Their pure black hearts

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.190
will finally be revealed!!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.230
Coming Soon!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.560
Understand?

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:52.240
This is what it is.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.880
I-I'm shocked.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.840
He made all those preparations just for this?

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:03.890
"If it's for the sake of seeing others suffer, no effort is too great." Is what the prince would say.

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:05.350
Got it.

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:06.980
Anyway, wake him up.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.720
I have something I want to say to him before I kill him.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:09.340
Do not.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:12.030
After all this crap you went through, aren't you upset?!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.330
Yes, I am upset!

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:19.060
But the King and Queen of Dogura, the prince's parents, are really good people!

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:23.900
Why must those two have birthed such a devil?

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.310
When I think of it, the sadness...

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:27.490
Oh, the sadness!

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:29.540
If you're gonna cry, quit already!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:38.020
Finally awake, you prankster prince?

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.720
I'm a female whose face screams <i>what</i> exactly?

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:44.420
Sorry, we screwed up.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:47.810
It looks like the gig was up before we arrived.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.550
"Ah" my ass, bitch.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.720
Don't you got somethin' to say, huh?

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.510
Like "I am very sorry."

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.080
Or "I went too far."

00:17:59.080 --> 00:17:59.690
Huh?

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:02.110
You peeked? How cruel!

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:04.490
That's the first thing you say?!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.410
"I like cats."

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:09.080
"If you want him, you're gonna have to go through me!"

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:14.730
Sorry, but I'm gonna have to kill him after all.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.410
Why is he laughing like a girl?

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.650
Don't come near me, idiot!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.480
Captain! C-Control yourself!

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:27.900
It's no use, Sade-kun!

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:30.210
I can't take it anymore!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.020
I don't care anymore!

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.560
Let's kill the bastard!

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.830
Haha!

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:36.670
Captain!

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.480
Captain!

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.920
Colin, hide yourself!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.040
R-Right!

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.830
I'm beat.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.990
A devil, huh?

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.100
Um...

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:01.890
W-What?

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:03.740
Um...

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:07.220
Can we have your autograph?

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:09.450
Huh?

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:13.710
You see, we Disckonians are huge baseball fans!

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:16.350
We check everything, from high school to college,

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:18.130
the pros, amateur leagues, everything!

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.730
The reason we don't go crazy on Earth is because it has baseball!

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:26.070
So the reason you wanted to observe Yukitaka-kun was...

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.050
Right!

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:30.870
You see, Osaka and Kanagawa, which have such strong baseball traditions,

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.990
are mostly under Ellerian territory!

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.090
They love baseball too.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:41.250
So it's rare for us to have a chance to see a future pro in the flesh!

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:46.550
We heard that a great hope from the best middle school team in Japan was entering Kisaragi!

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:47.500
That's why!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.050
Well, I wouldn't say that...

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.270
I was just a substitute...

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.640
Don't say that!

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:52.860
Chief said...

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.300
This one is the real deal.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:56.890
...and gave you his seal of approval!

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.620
T-Thanks...

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.720
Kisaragi's baseball team has gotten a lot of strong players recently.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.720
We're really hoping for good things!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.250
Work hard and head to the Koushien!

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.190
R-Right...

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:11.050
And then, with your strength,

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:15.410
the red flag of victory will finally break north of the Shirakawa Barrier to Yamagata!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:18.770
I'll do my best.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:20.460
Here.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.580
Thank you.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:24.740
It's my pleasure.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:27.950
Oh yes.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:32.260
He'll handle the damage to the wall, so no worries.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:34.380
He's also a Disckonian, see.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.470
Howdy.

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:41.630
Also, if you ever have any other issues with aliens, just call.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.410
We'll crush 'em right away.

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:52.840
Three months have passed since then.

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:03.960
It's okay! You can open it!

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.170
I've got news!

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:06.660
I-I...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.480
I've been chosen as a starter for the summer tournament, #7 left field!

00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:11.160
Really? Congratulations.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.030
Well, that's the good news.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.570
But there's something else.

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:17.420
A letter from far off...

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.930
And no postmark.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:22.500
You think it's that Prince Baka?

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:30.640
"I write this with regret that I had to leave Earth without so much as saying goodbye."

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.380
What a liar! That bastard doesn't give a damn!

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:38.740
"I was imprisoned during the entire conference and couldn't contact you."

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:39.660
"Sorry!"

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.030
"Thanks to my passionate advocacy, the conference was a great success."

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.170
"The Earth has been marked as a planet under Dogurian observation,"

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:51.880
"And I was appointed as head of the force tasked with maintaining security."

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:56.630
"In other words, Earth is now part of Dogura's domain."

00:21:56.630 --> 00:22:00.390
"The weight of such a responsibility lies heavily upon me."

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:04.380
"That being the case, in order for my job to go smoothly,"

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:07.010
"I will need to take up residence on Earth."

00:22:07.270 --> 00:22:09.400
"I'll pay you a visit soon."

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:10.470
No way...

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.210
Way. This guy's always...

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:16.600
...going above the diagonal.

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:27.650
Are you ready?

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:38.160
Do not fear 'The Now' searching for something that can't be seen across this infinite distance

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:52.380
Under the hundred million glittering lights, I found you searching for your dream

00:22:52.380 --> 00:23:01.140
An infinite world filled with glass shards

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:13.200
Growing up I felt I knew many meaningless things

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:20.660
Shining like a jewel, you soar in the sky, no past, no future

00:23:20.660 --> 00:23:26.000
The answer is beyond the sky

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:36.510
Do not fear 'The Dream', in a distant
place where truth and lies are unseen

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:52.240
Under the hundred million glittering lights, flowers sway in the wind

00:23:57.650 --> 00:24:00.250
I said, it's not something laugh about!

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:02.770
And we say we saw someone take the Yasuda's body,

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:07.110
suck out all their fluids, and eat even the skin and bones?

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:08.130
What'll we do?

00:24:08.130 --> 00:24:11.950
Is that monster in the same school as us?

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:15.350
Um... E course.

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:18.200
Next time: From the DARKNESS

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:20.540
Welcome. Have a seat.
